# Pairs with BackupSagaConsistent. Expiry removes the decision row instead of
# leaving it stored as a tombstone until the prune, so a saga whose terminal
# fan-out is half done loses its decision while one of its buckets is still
# pending. A capture then serves that bucket pre-saga beside a shard that
# already applied the commit. Production keeps the expired row until
# TxRegistryGrain.PruneExpired, which runs only after the saga forgot it,
# and the saga forgets only after its broadcast. DEADLOCK is off because the
# dropped row also strands the pending bucket for good: no sweep or
# broadcast can terminate it, so the saga never quiesces.
MODULE: BackupSagaConsistentExpiryDropsRow
TARGET: BackupSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an expired decision row is removed at expiry instead of at the prune
PERTURBS: Expire
DEADLOCK: off

--- FIND
    /\ expired' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<reg, deleg, epoch, prep, dec, loc, term>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ expired' = TRUE
    \* MUTATION: the row is dropped at expiry, before the terminals land.
    /\ loc' = [loc EXCEPT !["s"]["T1"] = "none"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<reg, deleg, epoch, prep, dec, term>>
--- END